Sanitized assignment patch summary for the Gemini connector stage.

This patch is limited to the assignment-specific changes made in this worker
run. It is intentionally not a full `git diff` against HEAD because the working
tree already contained unrelated documentation changes before this assignment.

Files changed:
- `model_bridge/gemini_runner.py`: new helper wrapping the official
  `google-genai` SDK client, `models.generate_content`, timeout execution,
  bounded output, usage/finish extraction, and sanitized error classification.
- `model_bridge/claude_bridge.py`: registers `ask_gemini`, loads
  `~/.codex/model-bridge/gemini.key` or `GEMINI_API_KEY_FILE`, keeps Gemini
  thread IDs provider-bound, records requests/responses in existing transcripts,
  and leaves project-worker routing unchanged.
- `pyproject.toml`: adds the `google-genai` dependency declaration.
- `tests/test_bridge.py`: adds mocked Gemini connector and runner coverage for
  mode/history separation, provider isolation, missing credentials, startup SDK
  failure, sanitized errors, timeout handling, usage/finish reporting, truncation,
  and MCP registration.
- `README.md`, `docs/OPERATIONS.md`, `docs/MCP_TOOL_SCHEMAS.json`,
  `docs/TASKS.md`: document the new tool, activation limits, exact schema, and
  task status.

Core MCP schema added:

```json
